adjudication.rationale:
In `addGuests.handler.ts`, email sending is wrapped in a `try/catch` that only `console.log`s (no rethrow, no error detail) and the handler still returns `{ message: "Guests added" }`:
```ts
try { await sendAddGuestsEmails(evt, guests); } catch (err) { console.log("Error sending AddGuestsEmails"); }
return { message: "Guests added" };
```
This can mask complete notification failure from the caller, but the core mutation (DB update + calendar update) has already succeeded, so it’s not strictly a correctness defect—more an API/observability/semantics concern introduced by the change.
